Dear Senator: I am not a politician, and do not know if recent elections or 'open enrollment' notifications are driving the motivation to NOT vote for the CR and keep the government closed.  As a healthcare operator, it's sad a sick.
• Open enrollment is not a one-day event.  A health plan patient notification is not an obligation of payment.  How do democrats expect to work with republicans and health plans to eliminate/minimize the increases for Americans that need financial help in 2026 with the government shut down?
• The insistence to add $1.5T dollars to the insanely broken healthcare system is pointless.  Senator, if you do not understand how healthcare works and how to fix it, do NOT just throw more money at it.  Humble yourself, solicit help, and partner with both parties on real solutions. 
• It's incredible to me that democrats are willing to "die on this hill" and allow federal workers to not be paid, only focusing on SNAP.  You don't think federal workers that don't get SNAP won't struggle to feed their families without a paycheck?
Please do better than this.  Vote for the CR and open the government. @LeaderJohnThune
